<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Ulus of Shiban</h1><p class="st-meta">1242 CE – 1428 CE (approx.) · capital Chimgi-Tura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The appanage of Jochi's son Shiban in western Siberia and the southern Urals, from which the Shaybanid dynasties of Bukhara and Khiva descended.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiban">Shiban</a>, a son of Jochi, distinguished himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu</a>'s western campaign of the late 1230s. In reward he received pastures east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-mountains">Urals</a>, in the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobol-river">Tobol</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tura-river">Tura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh</a>, as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shibanids</a> ruled nomadic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kipchaks">Kipchak</a> and Mongol tribes and Siberian forest peoples, collecting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyumen">Chimgi-Tura</a> (later Tyumen) as a seat. They acted as junior members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jochids">Jochid</a> house, taking part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde's</a> politics and civil wars in the 14th century, when several Shibanid princes claimed the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarai">Sarai</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> collapsed, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shibanid</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-khayr-khan">Abu'l-Khayr Khan</a> proclaimed himself khan in 1428, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uzbek-khanate">Uzbek Khanate</a>. Other Shibanids founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyumen-khanate">Tyumen Khanate</a>. Abu'l-Khayr's grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-shaybani">Muhammad Shaybani</a> later conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, establishing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-bukhara">Khanate of Bukhara</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1242 CE – 1428 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.42%;width:3.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1242 CE – 1428 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chimgi-Tura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shiban</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism, later Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kipchak Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>, <a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shibanid ulus, Shaybanid appanage</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1335&amp;focus=ulus-of-shiban" aria-label="Ulus of Shiban on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6089 240 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ulus of Shiban lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6409 496L6352 637M6409 496L6409 496"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6352 637h0M6409 496h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6409 49